// Drive a local harness PDS into enrolling with a real notification relay.
//
// The relay client is reactive: it enrolls only when a job needs the relay and the relay
// answers NotEnrolled. Booting a PDS with [notifications] configured therefore proves
// nothing — this produces the one job we can trigger by hand (a device registration) and
// reports what came back.
//
// Account creation goes through tools/interop's ceremony rather than plain XRPC, because
// Custos refuses to mint server-custodied identities: createAccount needs a client-signed
// did:plc genesis operation. That ceremony already exists; reimplementing it in curl would
// mean reimplementing the key custody model.
//
// Run: node notify-enroll-test.mjs      (needs `just interop-setup` once)

